### 🧪 ABOUT ALCH3MYOS

Alch3myOS is a meticulously crafted Android Custom ROM built to transcend hardware limitations & deliver a deeply optimized, high-performance experience across supported devices. We believe your smartphone should feel magical, which is why our ultimate goal is to provide a seamless, high-performance experience with carefully curated enhancements.

### 📦 SOURCE CODE & DEVICE TREES

Alch3myOS is proudly open-source. All of our device-specific configurations, hardware wrappers, & kernels are available on our GitHub organization.

* **Device Repositories:** [Alch3myOS-Devices](https://github.com/orgs/Alch3myOS-Devices/repositories)

---

### 🛠️ GETTING STARTED

### Prerequisites
* Git LFS installed globally (`git lfs install`).

### Initialize the Repository
Create a new working directory for your build, navigate to it, and initialize the Alch3myOS manifest:
```bash
repo init -u https://github.com/Alch3myOS/android -b 17 --git-lfs
```

### Sync the Source
```bash
repo sync -c --force-sync -j$(nproc --all)
```


### 🚀 COMPILING THE ROM

- Set up the build environment
```bash
. b*/env*
```

- Lunch your target device (replace codename with your device, e.g., husky or komodo):
```bash
lunch lineage_codename-bp4a-user
```

- Ensure recent changes build:
```bash
m installclean
```

- Start the compilation:
```bash
m bacon
```

### ⚙️ MAINTAINER CUSTOMIZATIONS

If you are setting up a new device tree for Alch3myOS, ensure the following flags and properties are set in your device's configuration files.

#### 1. Maintainer Info

Define the maintainer name & url so it reflects correctly in the OS. Add this to your device_name/product.prop
```prop
ro.alch3my.maintainer=Libra420T
```
```prop
ro.alch3my.maintainer.url=https://t.me/LibraAlch3my
```

#### 2. Device Info Overlay

To ensure the "About Phone" settings display the correct device aesthetics, create an RRO-overlay. Adapt the structure found in our reference repositories:

> **Reference:** [Alch3mySettingsHusky Overlay](https://github.com/Alch3myOS-Devices/device_google_shusky/tree/16/husky/overlay_packages/Alch3mySettingsHusky)

#### 3. Google Services (GMS)

Let's be real: We know most users want Google apps on their daily driver. Unless you are trying to win some kind of irony award by aggressively de-Googling your device, GMS is included. (Sorry no Vanilla releases)
